{
  "slug": "artist:dj-deeon",
  "name": "DJ Deeon",
  "editorial_article": "Chicago producer Deeon Boyd launched his influential career in 1994 with the 'Funk City' EP on the Dance Mania label. As a founding architect of the South Side's ghetto house sound, Boyd utilized a Roland TR-909 drum machine, often pushing the device to its limits to create high-energy, stripped-back percussion. His 1996 club classic 'Freak Like Me' became a defining anthem of the scene, famously earning him a mention in the Daft Punk song 'Teachers' in 1997. His vast discography spans decades, including later work for labels like Numbers and Teklife, where he released the 2021 project 'Destiny'. Before his death in 2023 at age 56, he remained prolific, dropping four EPs over a single weekend in May of that same year.",
